<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51146" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσόρροπ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥοπή</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>in equipoise</i>, of the balance, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				109a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Plt.</u>
				270a
			</span></i>(
				Sup.
			), etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάλαντα βρίσας οὐκ ἰσορρόπῳ τύχῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					346
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσορρόπου τοῦ πήχεως</span>
			(sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ ζυγοῦ</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> γινομένου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					22.1013.34
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>well-balanced, well-matched</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ.
				αὐτὸς ἑαυτῷ</span> of a man <i>with his legs of the
				same length</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				19
			</span></i>; of a nose, <i>flattened, but not awry</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Art.</u>
				37
			</span></i>; of a bone, <i>cylindrical</i>, ib. <i><span class="en">
				34
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέρμα ἰ</span>., opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιρρεπής</span>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				50
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. ἀγών</span>
			<i>evenly balanced</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				706
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάχη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.105
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυνάμεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					52e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					733c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιμή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1164b4
				</span></i>
			: c. dat., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ γένος τὸ Ἀττικὸν ἰ.
				τῷ ἑωυτῶν ἂν γίνοιτο</span> would become <i>a match
				for</i> their own, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.91
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. Ῥωμαίοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdn.
					6.7.8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. καταστῆναί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IPE</u>
					12.40.18
				</span></i>
			(Olbia, <span class="entity">ii A.D.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. ὁ
				λόγος τῶν ἔργων</span>
			<i>in precise equipoise with . . </i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.42
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdn.
					6.3.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>of equal weight</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσίον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Inscr.Délos</u>
					313a
				</span></i>
			.<i><span class="en">
				45
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ορο</span>-). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-όπως, ἀφιέναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Art.</u>
					43
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πορεύεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					247b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγωνίσασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					41.61
				</span></i>
			: neut. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσόρροπα</span> as
				Adv., <i><span class="en">
				Tim.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				47
			</span></i>.</div>
